{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/codex_memory.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project Research Memory\n\n## Goal And Phase\n- Phase 1 ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515 unmet; Phase 2 pending. server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one task per GPU; server-6 excluded.\n- Released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone and project decoder. No validation tuning of thresholds, temperatures, weights, features, margins or fixed 30-epoch protocol.\n- `research_on_capacity_gap=true`; six hard gates remain diagnosis, controls, native backward, resources, independence and constraints.\n\n## Champion And Baseline\n- B1 0.5020 mIoU, Acc@0.25 0.610, Acc@0.5 0.553, spmIoU 0.467.\n- B4-E30 champion 0.5094, Acc@0.25 0.608, Acc@0.5 0.562, spmIoU 0.474 at epoch 27; target gap 0.0056. B4-E30 continued epoch-20 optimizer/scheduler, not a fresh matched control.\n- B4-E30 best checkpoint: `/bak_home/songcl/Project/AdaRES_project/AdaRES_checkpoints/adares_b4_query_competition_res/20260921_210214/best.pth`.\n\n## Active Hypotheses\n- G1 changes seed/object indicator labels to detached per-query predicted-mask IoU against training targets. Fixed 16-scene B4 diagnosis: 37/240 material errors selected a positive lower-IoU query over a seed-negative oracle. Native backward/resource gates passed; full training outcome pending.\n- No other candidate passes admission. Fixed-subset oracle-mask quality greatly exceeds selected-mask quality, but that is not sufficient to infer a successful confidence mechanism.\n\n## Closed Or Failed Directions\n- B0 0.333; B2-E30 0.5058; B3 0.5014; B4 20-epoch 0.5070; B5 0.5030; C1-E30 0.5008; C2-E30 0.5014; F4 0.5060; D1 0.5080. No tuning-only, seed-repeat or extension-only successor.\n- H5 late global query attention ended 2026-09-26 13:47 +08:00 at best 0.5061 after 30 validations and protected early stop; below B4-E30 by 0.0033. The process had not completed all final training steps. Auxiliary terminal metrics unavailable after monitor log-pull failure.\n- E1 stability, F1 entropy, F2 compactness, F3 seed proximity rejected. H1 sampler omission (0/240), H2 balanced shortlist reduced coverage, H3 score-only 0.38265 versus indicator 0.49186 subset mIoU, H4 relation cohort not enriched; all rejected.\n- J1 pooled mask-language contrast: oracle higher in 123/240 material errors, standalone subset mIoU 0.01315; J2 overlap crowding: oracle higher in 78/240, selected mean crowding 7.936 versus oracle 6.487. Both rejected after fixed 16-scene native screens.\n- K1 sampler-rank shortcut: oracle later in 141/240, higher sampler score in 99/240; sampler-only mIoU 0.34587. K2 mask-area shortcut: oracle larger in 118/240; largest-mask mIoU 0.27271. B4 fixed subset mIoU 0.49186. Both rejected after native 16-scene screens.\n- L1 mask-interior coherence: oracle higher 116/240, standalone mIoU 0.13079. L2 local boundary contrast: oracle higher 104/240, standalone mIoU 0.25651 versus B4 subset 0.49186. Rejected at diagnosis; no backward/resource or admission.\n\n## Running And Queue\n- Prepared 2026-09-26 15:47 +08:00 monitor: G1 marked running server-2 GPU0 with deathwatch 1/3; one active of two, no waiting/claiming, candidate budget one. Prior 14:47 snapshot had G1 29/30, interim best 0.4983.\n- Targeted live query: server-2 GPU0 and GPU1 each 1 MiB, 0%; no G1 training process. Do not infer terminal status or manually mutate queue; scheduled monitor reconciles deathwatch.\n- G1 commit `0f5f695d478b87750d69561428f6421833e629a9`, admission receipt and launch-progress verification recorded. No new candidate enqueued.\n- `research_work.json` latest design cycle attempted L1 and L2, admitted zero, with SHA256 evidence and concrete stop/resume conditions. No due pending candidate.\n\n## Open Questions And Risks\n- No pending questions in prepared manifest. G1 terminal outcome, active queries, full-run latency/peak memory, subgroup effects and evaluation noise remain unknown.\n- H5 30/30 validations did not mean 30 complete training epochs; monitor killed mid-final epoch after patience threshold. Remote log pull failed, so H5 secondary metrics were not inferred.\n- Local Python lacks PyTorch; L1/L2 diagnostics ran in native server-2 environment GPU1. The script was copied for read-only research outside the training tree; no candidate code sync or dispatch.\n- The fixed 16-scene screens are observational, not population or causal efficacy estimates. Negative routes do not establish global hypothesis exhaustion. Resume new independent route with diagnosis and controls, or when G1 terminates.\n\n## Last Tick\n- 2026-09-26 16:00 +08:00 design: monitor and goal preflight succeeded before Codex and were not rerun. L1/L2 native screens rejected, no admission. Analysis, motivation review, design and route decision recorded. Scheduled monitor should reconcile G1 deathwatch.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
