{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/decisions/20260926-160022_route_change.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1-L2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-155700.md'\"","aggregated_output":"Get-Content: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Cont …\r\n     |  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n     | 找不到路径“D:\\project\\AdaRES_project\\pipeline\\references\\autonomous_design.md”，因为该路径不存在。\r\n# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 16:00:22\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: Can mask-interior coherence or local boundary contrast explain B4 selection errors enough to admit one candidate?\n- **决策**: Reject L1 and L2 after native fixed-subset screens; leave server-2 GPU1 vacant and let normal monitor reconcile G1 deathwatch.\n- **依据**: L1 oracle higher 116/240 and standalone mIoU 0.13079; L2 oracle higher 104/240 and standalone mIoU 0.25651 versus B4 subset 0.49186; both fail diagnosis.\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-L1-L2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-155700.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Fixed native screens: mask feature coherence and local boundary contrast\n\n2026-09-26 15:57 Asia/Shanghai. B4-E30 best checkpoint, first 16 ScanRefer validation scenes, 441 expressions and 240 material selection errors (oracle minus selected mask IoU > 0.05). Read-only native server-2 GPU1 inference; no training state or queue changes. Paired rows: `AdaRES-L1_native_16scenes_20260926.json` and `AdaRES-L2_native_16scenes_20260926.json`. Script: `AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_l1_feature_consistency.py`.\n\n| Route | Predeclared mechanism | Paired evidence and standalone controls | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 mask-interior feature coherence | Better target masks should cover visually consistent superpoints, and B4's query-only competition head misses this mask-conditioned quality. | Oracle soft-mask coherence higher in 116/240 material errors; mean oracle 0.99606 versus selected 0.99623. Soft-coherence-only mIoU 0.13079, hard-mask coherence-only 0.04867 in the first run, versus B4 0.49186. | Reject the proposed directional coherence mechanism. No feature weighting or threshold search. |\n| L2 local feature boundary contrast | Better target masks should place boundaries across stronger local feature discontinuities than wrongly selected masks. | Oracle boundary score higher in 104/240 errors; mean oracle 0.04582 versus selected 0.04924. Boundary-only mIoU 0.25651 versus B4 0.49186. Eight nearest spatial neighbors per superpoint, hard predicted mask, difference of mean crossing and non-crossing feature dissimilarities. | Reject this local-boundary mechanism as stated. No k-neighbor or score-fusion scan. |\n\nL1's native run used an unmodified coherence probe. L2 added boundary measurement and reran the same cohort; its hard-coherence-only mIoU was 0.04984, a minor tie-sensitive difference. The scene features are final decoder scene features, not an independent vision oracle. These validation-subset observations are not population efficacy estimates. Both directions fail the diagnosis hard gate; candidate-specific native backward, training resources, independence and admission are not claimed. G1's terminal state is still pending monitor reconciliation.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
